  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Fructose 1,6-Diphosphate and 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, mediated through a series of targets. Fructose 1,6-Diphosphate is identified as a target of multiple compounds, including CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which in turn is targeted by 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide, (+)-(5S,7R)-7-Ethoxy-12-Hydroxy-2-Oxo-20-Norabieta-1(10),8,11,13-Tetraene, and Zizyberenalic acid. These compounds all appear to interact with the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, indicating a possible pathway where Fructose 1,6-Diphosphate serves as a precursor or modulator in the regulation of this subunit. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains unclear. The evidence highlights a network of targets and compounds that may influence the proteasome subunit, but further research is needed to elucidate the precise role of Fructose 1,6-Diphosphate in this process.",
